From cd9b9a17c8a432c697574be54705d1c62f26f9dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:04:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] fix(fixtures): derive reference profiles only from STEP
 fixtures

DeriveFixtureProfile replaced the generating profile of a DXF/profile
fixture with a bulge-free derived polygon. The chord bound fell to zero,
the fixture became mesh-eligible, and mesh refinement cleared a real
collision with the intended curved steel. On an imported mesh fixture,
library re-insertion would re-mesh from the derived approximation.

Derivation is now refused by name for every fixture without a STEP
source. Pinned by
generated_fixture_refuses_reference_derivation_and_keeps_its_collision_bound,
mesh_fixture_without_step_source_refuses_reference_derivation and
mcp_derive_fixture_profile_refuses_generated_fixture_and_keeps_its_profile.

Refs #744

